{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ADR57PjY4D4qbrAfRtXVb4","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"canonical_task\": {\n    \"path\": \"task.md\",\n    \"sha256\": \"e4935f14c47be3f40dba4b1e04f0cc983f4d8d35b139befe19b98f5b4ec88e67\"\n  },\n  \"method\": {\n    \"class\": \"Evaluator-verified, budgeted data-dropping sensitivity analysis of Bradley-Terry pairwise-comparison leaderboards: the candidate receives an anonymized comparison table plus a target ranking event and a removal cap, and proposes a set of comparisons to delete (influence-guided search with refit-based refinement is the intended direction); the evaluator refits Bradley-Terry exactly on the remaining data and verifies whether the target ranking event flipped.\",\n    \"description\": \"Candidate exposes handle(request) over python_rpc_v1. Per episode: op=reset (seed), op=load_chunk (<=4 base64 chunks of an anonymized uint16/uint16/uint8 comparison table), op=analyze (target adjacent pair hi/lo, removal cap k_cap=ceil(0.02 N), Bradley-Terry definition fields) returning base64 uint32 row indices to delete. The evaluator refits Bradley-Terry exactly (float64 Newton, ridge 0.01, ties as half wins) and scores 1-k/k_cap when the target order flips. Claim: On the declared real datasets only (search: Chatbot Arena crowd votes arena-55k and MT-Bench expert human judgments; final: Chatbot Arena crowd votes arena-140k after content-hash deduplication against search data, and NBA game results as a sports design), and for the declared target events (point-estimate order reversal of one adjacent top-of-table pair and one adjacent mid-table pair under a removal cap of 2% of comparisons), a refit-verified influence-guided removal search finds a ranking flip with a smaller removal fraction than the evaluator-owned random-removal and first-order-influence-only baselines, and the minimum verified flip fraction differs (or does not differ) across evaluation designs. This is a bounded descriptive claim about the declared cases; it does not cover confidence-interval-based rank changes, insertion/flipping/adversarial vote rigging, other datasets, other rating models, or causal explanations of why designs differ. 'Sensitivity is small', 'depends on conditions' and 'differs from expectation' are equally acceptable final outcomes; the final assessment reports baseline comparisons per case with paired per-case differences and bootstrap intervals over episodes as descriptive uncertainty, not as significance tests over a population of datasets.\"\n  },\n  \"candidate\": {\n    \"interface\": \"python_rpc_v1:handle\",\n    \"editable_paths\": [\n      \"program_0/src\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"evaluators\": {\n    \"search\": \"evaluate.py\",\n    \"final\": \"evaluate_final.py\"\n  },\n  \"resources\": {\n    \"search_root\": \"resources/search\",\n    \"final_root\": \"resources/final\",\n    \"public_artifact_bundle\": null\n  },\n  \"data\": {\n    \"search_roles\": [\n      \"search_pairwise_comparisons\"\n    ],\n    \"final_roles\": [\n      \"final_pairwise_comparisons\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"metrics\": {\n    \"search\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"combined_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_pairwise_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"flip_rate\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_pairwise_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"mean_budget_fraction\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_pairwise_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"score_crowd\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_pairwise_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"score_expert\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_pairwise_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"reference_random_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_pairwise_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"reference_influence_score\",\n        \"data_role\": \"search_pairwise_comparisons\"\n      },\n      {